class MultiViewFusionNode(Node):
    """
    Step13.4.5 v1.2
    Self-correcting lightweight online multi-view fusion.

    Main idea:
        - keep a stable reference AXIS for branch identity/orientation
        - do NOT permanently lock the branch LENGTH to the first frame
        - axial endpoints may expand only after repeated support from
          several valid frames
        - maintain a rolling window of recent valid observations
        - ACCEPT and IGNORE frames both contribute geometric evidence
        - build the fused cloud from cross-frame support rather than
          permanently appending points
        - use robust radial pruning to remove unsupported penetration /
          background tails
        - slowly adapt the reference axis from the cleaned rolling model

    This keeps the previous identity / endpoint safeguards, while allowing
    an early imperfect model to be corrected by later multi-view evidence.

    No ICP / TSDF / heavy PCL pipeline is required.
    """

